Reasoning

Here is a complete, self-contained, single-file HTML application. It requires no internet connection, no external libraries, and no live web lookups. It runs entirely in your browser and auto-saves your work to local storage.

How to use:
Copy the code block below.
Save it as editor-flipbook.html on your desktop or tablet.
Open the file in any modern browser (Chrome, Safari, Edge, Firefox).
html
<!DOCTYPE html>

<html lang="en">

<head>

    <meta charset="UTF-8">

    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>Research Claim Flipbook & Handoff Tool</title>

    <style>

        :root {

            --bg-color: #f8f9fa;

            --card-bg: #ffffff;

            --text-primary: #212529;

            --text-secondary: #6c757d;

            --accent: #2563eb;

            --accent-hover: #1d4ed8;

            --risk-low: #16a34a;

            --risk-medium: #ca8a04;

            --risk-high: #dc2626;

            --border: #dee2e6;

            --shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);

        }



        * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

        body {

            font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;

            background-color: var(--bg-color);

            color: var(--text-primary);

            line-height: 1.6;

            padding: 20px;

            max-width: 900px;

            margin: 0 auto;

        }



        header {

            text-align: center;

            margin-bottom: 30px;

            padding-bottom: 20px;

            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);

        }

        header h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }

        header p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.95rem; }



        /* Tabs */

        .tabs { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }

        .tab-btn {

            padding: 10px 20px;

            background: none;

            border: none;

            border-bottom: 3px solid transparent;

            cursor: pointer;

            font-size: 1rem;

            font-weight: 600;

            color: var(--text-secondary);

            transition: all 0.2s;

        }

        .tab-btn.active { color: var(--accent); border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }

        .tab-btn:hover { color: var(--accent); }



        .tab-content { display: none; animation: fadeIn 0.3s ease; }

        .tab-content.active { display: block; }



        @keyframes fadeIn { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(5px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }



        /* Forms */

        .form-group { margin-bottom: 16px; }

        label { display: block; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 0.9rem; }

        input, select, textarea {

            width: 100%;

            padding: 10px 12px;

            border: 1px solid var(--border);

            border-radius: 6px;

            font-size: 1rem;

            font-family: inherit;

            transition: border-color 0.2s;

        }

        input:focus, select:focus, textarea:focus {

            outline: none;

            border-color: var(--accent);

            box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.1);

        }

        textarea { min-height: 100px; resize: vertical; }



        .btn {

            display: inline-flex;

            align-items: center;

            justify-content: center;

            padding: 10px 20px;

            background-color: var(--accent);

            color: white;

            border: none;

            border-radius: 6px;

            font-size: 1rem;

            font-weight: 600;

            cursor: pointer;

            transition: background-color 0.2s;

            gap: 8px;

        }

        .btn:hover { background-color: var(--accent-hover); }

        .btn-secondary { background-color: var(--text-secondary); }

        .btn-secondary:hover { background-color: #495057; }

        .btn-danger { background-color: var(--risk-high); }

        .btn-danger:hover { background-color: #b91c1c; }



        /* Flipbook Viewer */

        .flipbook-controls {

            display: flex;

            justify-content: space-between;

            align-items: center;

            margin-bottom: 20px;

            flex-wrap: wrap;

            gap: 10px;

        }

        .toggle-label {

            display: flex;

            align-items: center;

            gap: 8px;

            font-size: 0.95rem;

            cursor: pointer;

            user-select: none;

        }



        .card-container {

            perspective: 1000px;

            min-height: 400px;

            display: flex;

            align-items: center;

            justify-content: center;

        }

        .flip-card {

            background: var(--card-bg);

            border-radius: 12px;

            box-shadow: var(--shadow);

            padding: 30px;

            width: 100%;

            max-width: 700px;

            position: relative;

            transition: transform 0.4s ease, opacity 0.4s ease;

            border-left: 6px solid var(--border);

        }

        .flip-card.risk-low { border-left-color: var(--risk-low); }

        .flip-card.risk-medium { border-left-color: var(--risk-medium); }

        .flip-card.risk-high { border-left-color: var(--risk-high); }



        .card-header {

            display: flex;

            justify-content: space-between;

            align-items: flex-start;

            margin-bottom: 20px;

            padding-bottom: 15px;

            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);

        }

        .risk-badge {

            padding: 4px 12px;

            border-radius: 20px;

            font-size: 0.8rem;

            font-weight: 700;

            text-transform: uppercase;

            letter-spacing: 0.5px;

            color: white;

        }

        .risk-low .risk-badge { background-color: var(--risk-low); }

        .risk-medium .risk-badge { background-color: var(--risk-medium); }

        .risk-high .risk-badge { background-color: var(--risk-high); }



        .claim-text {

            font-size: 1.25rem;

            font-weight: 500;

            margin-bottom: 20px;

            line-height: 1.5;

        }

        .meta-grid {

            display: grid;

            grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;

            gap: 15px;

            margin-bottom: 20px;

            font-size: 0.95rem;

        }

        .meta-item strong { display: block; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.85rem; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 4px; }

        .freshness-warning {

            background-color: #fef3c7;

            color: #92400e;

            padding: 10px 15px;

            border-radius: 6px;

            font-size: 0.9rem;

            margin-top: 15px;

            display: flex;

            align-items: center;

            gap: 8px;

        }

        .freshness-warning.critical {

            background-color: #fee2e2;

            color: #991b1b;

        }



        .card-nav {

            display: flex;

            justify-content: center;

            gap: 15px;

            margin-top: 25px;

        }

        .empty-state {

            text-align: center;

            padding: 60px 20px;

            color: var(--text-secondary);

        }



        /* Export Section */

        .export-area {

            width: 100%;

            min-height: 300px;

            font-family: "SF Mono", Monaco, "Cascadia Code", "Roboto Mono", Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;

            font-size: 0.9rem;

            line-height: 1.5;

            padding: 15px;

            background-color: #f1f5f9;

            border: 1px solid var(--border);

            border-radius: 6px;

            resize: vertical;

            margin-bottom: 15px;

        }



        .math-note {

            font-size: 0.85rem;

            color: var(--text-secondary);

            background: #eef2ff;

            padding: 12px;

            border-radius: 6px;

            margin-top: 20px;

            border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);

        }



        @media (max-width: 600px) {

            .meta-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }

            .flipbook-controls { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }

            body { padding: 15px; }

        }

    </style>

</head>

<body>



<header>

    <h1>📚 Research Claim Flipbook</h1>

    <p>Paste claims, tag evidence, assess freshness risk, and generate clean editor handoffs. 100% offline.</p>

</header>



<div class="tabs">

    <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab('input')">1. Add Claims</button>

    <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab('flipbook')">2. Review Flipbook</button>

    <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab('export')">3. Editor Handoff</button>

</div>



<!-- TAB 1: INPUT -->

<div id="tab-input" class="tab-content active">

    <form id="claimForm">

        <div class="form-group">

            <label for="claim">Claim / Quote</label>

            <textarea id="claim" placeholder="e.g., 'Intermittent fasting reduces cardiovascular risk by 20%.'" required></textarea>

        </div>

        <div class="form-group">

            <label for="source">Source Note / Citation</label>

            <input type="text" id="source" placeholder="e.g., Smith et al., NEJM, 2019" required>

        </div>

        <div class="meta-grid">

            <div class="form-group">

                <label for="pubDate">Publication Date</label>

                <input type="date" id="pubDate" required>

            </div>

            <div class="form-group">

                <label for="evidenceType">Evidence Type</label>

                <select id="evidenceType" required>

                    <option value="meta-analysis">Meta-Analysis / Systematic Review</option>

                    <option value="rct">Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)</option>

                    <option value="observational">Observational / Cohort Study</option>

                    <option value="expert">Expert Opinion / Editorial</option>

                    <option value="anecdotal">Anecdotal / Unknown / Blog</option>

                </select>

            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="form-group">

            <label for="notes">Editor Notes (Optional)</label>

            <textarea id="notes" placeholder="e.g., Check if this conflicts with the 2023 WHO guidelines." style="min-height: 60px;"></textarea>

        </div>

        <button type="submit" class="btn">➕ Add to Flipbook</button>

    </form>



    <div class="math-note">

        <strong>How Risk is Calculated:</strong> 

        Total Risk Score $R = A + E$, where $A$ is the Age Penalty ($0$ if $\le 2$ years, $+1$ if $2-5$ years, $+2$ if $>5$ years) and $E$ is the Evidence Penalty (Meta-analysis $= 0$, RCT $= 1$, Observational $= 2$, Expert $= 3$, Anecdotal $= 4$). 

        Risk levels: $R \le 1$ (Low), $2 \le R \le 3$ (Medium), $R \ge 4$ (High).

    </div>

</div>



<!-- TAB 2: FLIPBOOK -->

<div id="tab-flipbook" class="tab-content">

    <div class="flipbook-controls">

        <div>

            <span id="cardCounter" style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-secondary);">0 / 0</span>

        </div>

        <div style="display: flex; gap: 15px; align-items: center;">

            <label class="toggle-label">

                <input type="checkbox" id="sortRiskToggle" onchange="renderFlipbook()">

                Sort by Highest Risk First

            </label>

            <button class="btn btn-danger" onclick="clearAllData()" style="padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.85rem;">Clear All</button>

        </div>

    </div>



    <div class="card-container" id="cardContainer">

        <!-- Cards injected here via JS -->

    </div>



    <div class="card-nav" id="cardNav" style="display: none;">

        <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="prevCard()">← Previous</button>

        <button class="btn" onclick="nextCard()">Next →</button>

    </div>

</div>



<!-- TAB 3: EXPORT -->

<div id="tab-export" class="tab-content">

    <p style="margin-bottom: 15px; color: var(--text-secondary);">This generates a clean, structured Markdown-ready handoff for your editorial CMS or team.</p>

    <textarea id="exportText" class="export-area" readonly></textarea>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px;">

        <button class="btn" onclick="copyToClipboard()">📋 Copy to Clipboard</button>

        <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="generateExport()">🔄 Regenerate</button>

    </div>

    <p id="copyFeedback" style="color: var(--risk-low); font-weight: 600; margin-top: 10px; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.3s;">Copied successfully!</p>

</div>



<script>

    // --- STATE MANAGEMENT ---

    let claims = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('research_claims')) || [];

    let currentIndex = 0;



    // --- TAB SWITCHING ---

    function switchTab(tabName) {

        document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content').forEach(el => el.classList.remove('active'));

        document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn').forEach(el => el.classList.remove('active'));



        document.getElementById(`tab-${tabName}`).classList.add('active');

        event.target.classList.add('active');



        if (tabName === 'flipbook') renderFlipbook();

        if (tabName === 'export') generateExport();

    }



    // --- RISK CALCULATION ---

    function calculateRisk(pubDateStr, evidenceType) {

        const pubDate = new Date(pubDateStr);

        const now = new Date();

        const yearsOld = (now - pubDate) / (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24 * 365.25);



        let agePenalty = 0;

        let freshnessWarning = null;



        if (yearsOld > 5) {

            agePenalty = 2;

            freshnessWarning = "Critical: Source is over 5 years old. Verify if newer data supersedes this.";

        } else if (yearsOld > 2) {

            agePenalty = 1;

            freshnessWarning = "Warning: Source is 2-5 years old. Consider checking for recent updates.";

        }



        const evidenceScores = {

            'meta-analysis': 0,

            'rct': 1,

            'observational': 2,

            'expert': 3,

            'anecdotal': 4

        };

        const evidencePenalty = evidenceScores[evidenceType] || 0;

        const totalRisk = agePenalty + evidencePenalty;



        let riskLevel = 'low';

        if (totalRisk >= 4) riskLevel = 'high';

        else if (totalRisk >= 2) riskLevel = 'medium';



        return { totalRisk, riskLevel, yearsOld: yearsOld.toFixed(1), freshnessWarning };

    }



    // --- FORM HANDLING ---

    document.getElementById('claimForm').addEventListener('submit', function(e) {

        e.preventDefault();



        const claim = document.getElementById('claim').value.trim();

        const source = document.getElementById('source').value.trim();

        const pubDate = document.getElementById('pubDate').value;

        const evidenceType = document.getElementById('evidenceType').value;

        const notes = document.getElementById('notes').value.trim();



        const riskData = calculateRisk(pubDate, evidenceType);



        const newClaim = {

            id: Date.now(),

            claim,

            source,

            pubDate,

            evidenceType,

            notes,

            riskScore: riskData.totalRisk,

            riskLevel: riskData.riskLevel,

            freshnessWarning: riskData.freshnessWarning,

            yearsOld: riskData.yearsOld

        };



        claims.push(newClaim);

        saveData();



        // Reset form

        this.reset();

        document.getElementById('claim').focus();



        alert('Claim added successfully! Switch to the "Review Flipbook" tab to view it.');

    });



    function saveData() {

        localStorage.setItem('research_claims', JSON.stringify(claims));

    }



    function clearAllData() {

        if (confirm('Are you sure you want to delete all claims? This cannot be undone.')) {

            claims = [];

            currentIndex = 0;

            saveData();

            renderFlipbook();

        }

    }



    // --- FLIPBOOK RENDERING ---

    function getSortedClaims() {

        const sortRisk = document.getElementById('sortRiskToggle').checked;

        if (sortRisk) {

            return [...claims].sort((a, b) => b.riskScore - a.riskScore);

        }

        return claims;

    }



    function renderFlipbook() {

        const container = document.getElementById('cardContainer');

        const nav = document.getElementById('cardNav');

        const counter = document.getElementById('cardCounter');

        const sortedClaims = getSortedClaims();



        if (sortedClaims.length === 0) {

            container.innerHTML = `

                <div class="empty-state">

                    <h3>No claims added yet.</h3>

                    <p>Go to the "Add Claims" tab to paste your first research claim.</p>

                </div>

            `;

            nav.style.display = 'none';

            counter.textContent = '0 / 0';

            return;

        }



        // Ensure currentIndex is valid

        if (currentIndex >= sortedClaims.length) currentIndex = sortedClaims.length - 1;

        if (currentIndex < 0) currentIndex = 0;



        const item = sortedClaims[currentIndex];

        counter.textContent = `${currentIndex + 1} / ${sortedClaims.length}`;

        nav.style.display = 'flex';



        const evidenceLabels = {

            'meta-analysis': 'Meta-Analysis / Systematic Review',

            'rct': 'Randomized Controlled Trial (RCT)',

            'observational': 'Observational / Cohort Study',

            'expert': 'Expert Opinion / Editorial',

            'anecdotal': 'Anecdotal / Unknown / Blog'

        };



        const warningHtml = item.freshnessWarning 

            ? `<div class="freshness-warning ${item.riskLevel === 'high' ? 'critical' : ''}">⚠️ ${item.freshnessWarning}</div>` 

            : `<div class="freshness-warning" style="background-color: #dcfce7; color: #166534;">✅ Source is fresh (${item.yearsOld} years old).</div>`;



        container.innerHTML = `

            <div class="flip-card risk-${item.riskLevel}" id="activeCard">

                <div class="card-header">

                    <span class="risk-badge">Risk: ${item.riskLevel.toUpperCase()} (Score: ${item.riskScore})</span>

                    <button class="btn btn-danger" style="padding: 4px 10px; font-size: 0.8rem;" onclick="deleteClaim(${item.id})">Delete</button>

                </div>

                <div class="claim-text">"${item.claim}"</div>

                <div class="meta-grid">

                    <div class="meta-item">

                        <strong>Source</strong>

                        ${item.source}

                    </div>

                    <div class="meta-item">

                        <strong>Evidence Type</strong>

                        ${evidenceLabels[item.evidenceType]}

                    </div>

                    <div class="meta-item">

                        <strong>Publication Date</strong>

                        ${new Date(item.pubDate).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' })}

                    </div>

                    <div class="meta-item">

                        <strong>Age</strong>

                        ${item.yearsOld} years

                    </div>

                </div>

                ${warningHtml}

                ${item.notes ? `<div style="margin-top: 20px; padding-top: 15px; border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);"><strong>Editor Notes:</strong> ${item.notes}</div>` : ''}

            </div>

        `;

    }



    function nextCard() {

        const sortedClaims = getSortedClaims();

        if (currentIndex < sortedClaims.length - 1) {

            currentIndex++;

            animateCardTransition('left');

        }

    }



    function prevCard() {

        if (currentIndex > 0) {

            currentIndex--;

            animateCardTransition('right');

        }

    }



    function animateCardTransition(direction) {

        const card = document.getElementById('activeCard');

        card.style.opacity = '0';

        card.style.transform = direction === 'left' ? 'translateX(-20px) rotateY(-5deg)' : 'translateX(20px) rotateY(5deg)';



        setTimeout(() => {

            renderFlipbook();

            const newCard = document.getElementById('activeCard');

            newCard.style.opacity = '0';

            newCard.style.transform = direction === 'left' ? 'translateX(20px) rotateY(5deg)' : 'translateX(-20px) rotateY(-5deg)';



            // Force reflow

            void newCard.offsetWidth; 



            newCard.style.opacity = '1';

            newCard.style.transform = 'translateX(0) rotateY(0)';

        }, 200);

    }



    function deleteClaim(id) {

        if (confirm('Delete this claim?')) {

            claims = claims.filter(c => c.id !== id);

            if (currentIndex >= claims.length) currentIndex = Math.max(0, claims.length - 1);

            saveData();

            renderFlipbook();

        }

    }



    // --- EXPORT HANDOFF ---

    function generateExport() {

        const sortedClaims = getSortedClaims();

        if (sortedClaims.length === 0) {

            document.getElementById('exportText').value = 'No claims to export.';

            return;

        }



        let output = `# RESEARCH CLAIMS HANDOFF\n`;

        output += `Generated: ${new Date().toLocaleString()}\n`;

        output += `Total Claims: ${sortedClaims.length}\n`;

        output += `Sort Order: ${document.getElementById('sortRiskToggle').checked ? 'Highest Risk First' : 'Chronological (Added)'}\n\n`;

        output += `---\n\n`;



        sortedClaims.forEach((item, index) => {

            output += `### Claim ${index + 1} [${item.riskLevel.toUpperCase()} RISK]\n`;

            output += `**Claim:** "${item.claim}"\n`;

            output += `**Source:** ${item.source}\n`;

            output += `**Date:** ${item.pubDate} (${item.yearsOld} years old)\n`;

            output += `**Evidence:** ${item.evidenceType}\n`;

            if (item.freshnessWarning) {

                output += `**⚠️ Freshness Note:** ${item.freshnessWarning}\n`;

            }

            if (item.notes) {

                output += `**Editor Notes:** ${item.notes}\n`;

            }

            output += `\n`;

        });



        document.getElementById('exportText').value = output;

    }



    function copyToClipboard() {

        const exportText = document.getElementById('exportText');

        exportText.select();

        exportText.setSelectionRange(0, 99999); // For mobile



        navigator.clipboard.writeText(exportText.value).then(() => {

            const feedback = document.getElementById('copyFeedback');

            feedback.style.opacity = '1';

            setTimeout(() => { feedback.style.opacity = '0'; }, 2000);

        }).catch(err => {

            alert('Failed to copy. Please select and copy manually.');

        });

    }



    // Initialize

    if (claims.length > 0) {

        // Keep default tab, but ensure state is ready

    }

</script>



</body>

</html>
Key Features of This Tool:
Self-Contained & Offline: Zero external dependencies. Save the .html file and it works forever on any desktop or tablet browser without internet.
Auto-Save: Uses localStorage so if you accidentally close the tab, your claims are still there when you reopen the file.
Algorithmic Risk Scoring: Automatically calculates a risk score R=A+E based on publication age and evidence hierarchy, color-coding cards (Green/Yellow/Red).
True Flipbook UX: Features smooth CSS 3D-style transitions when navigating Previous/Next, optimized for both mouse clicks and tablet touch taps.
Priority Sorting: Toggle "Sort by Highest Risk First" in the flipbook view to immediately audit the most fragile citations.
Clean Handoff Export: Generates a structured, Markdown-formatted text block ready to be pasted directly into Notion, Google Docs, WordPress, or your editorial CMS with one click.

Reasoning

Here is the completely rewritten, security-hardened version of the tool. It strictly uses addEventListener for all interactions and document.createElement with textContent for all user-entered data, eliminating XSS risks and ensuring it passes strict editorial review gates.

